+## Carrier Talk sessions
+
+<a id="api-runtime-realtimevoice" />
+
+`api.runtime.realtimeVoice.createSession(params)` lets a bundled or trusted official
+carrier provide audio to the same host-owned Talk conversation used by native clients.
+It inherits Talk configuration, provider authentication, conversation history, agent
+reasoning and tools, transcript persistence, and native run controls. It does not
+accept carrier-specific model or agent-policy overrides.
+
+Supply a stable `callId`, optional canonical `sessionKey`, an `owner` with a handle
+and `assertCurrent()` admission check, a call lifetime `signal`, and an `audioSink`.
+The assertion must recheck the same live call and authenticated allowlisted owner.
+The host also checks plugin and Gateway lifetime; a retained capability fails after
+its owner retires. The carrier identity does not fabricate a WebSocket client or
+operator credentials. Media can supply `audioFormat` and provider event callbacks.
+
+The result exposes the bridge media methods, canonical `sessionKey`, `voiceSessionId`,
+and `providerId`. Call `connect()` to start media. Ordinary `close()` detaches accepted
+native work, drains final provider transcripts, and closes the media owner. Explicit
+agent cancellation remains a separate native control operation. Accepted work may
+finish in the shared chat after the call ends.
+
+An optional `onHangupRequested` callback handles an explicit current-call hangup
+command. It requests carrier termination; the carrier still confirms its actual call
+end before closing media. A hangup request prevents new agent admission but does not
+cancel work already accepted. Callback failures are reported through `onError`.
+
